{
  "dom_id": "question-341780",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "Let $f(x)$ be the $2L$-periodic extension of a function $F(x)$ from $x\\in [-L,L)$ to $x\\in R.$\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nThe Fourier series of $f$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({{field-1}})+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({{field-2}}).\n$$\n\nThe $7$th sine coefficient of the series is\n\n$$\n{b}_{7}={{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nGiven that $F(x)=x$ and $L=2\\pi ,$ the $7$th sine coefficient becomes\n\n$$\n{b}_{7}={{field-4}}\\,\\cdot \\,{{field-5}}.\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
